Artifact Requirements (ESOP 2026 - Artifact)

Packaged Architectures
----------------------
This artifact is packaged as pre-built Docker images for the following architectures:

1) linux/amd64 (x86_64)
   Image archive: templates-artifact-amd64-built.tar.gz

2) linux/arm64 (AArch64)
   Image archive: templates-artifact-arm64-built.tar.gz


Software Requirements
---------------------
Required:
- Docker Engine (tested with Docker Desktop and Docker Engine)
- A Linux environment, or macOS/Windows with Docker Desktop

Notes for Windows:
- We recommend using Docker Desktop with WSL2 backend for best performance.


Hardware Requirements
---------------------
Minimum:
- CPU: 4 cores
- RAM: 16 GB
- Storage: 35+ GB free disk space (Docker image is large)

Recommended:
- CPU: 8+ cores
- RAM: 32 GB
- Storage: 50+ GB free disk space

Non-commodity peripherals:
- None required.


Performance Notes
-----------------
- Building/checking the Rocq/VST proofs inside Docker can take significant time on some machines.
- If compilation is slow, reduce parallelism (e.g., `make -j2` or `make -j3`).


Machine-Readable Dependency Files
---------------------------------
The artifact includes the following machine-readable dependency specifications:
- Dockerfile (for building the container environment)
- opam files / Rocq toolchain configuration inside the container (used to install Rocq/Coq packages)
- Makefiles under:
  - template-implementations/ (C implementations)
  - template-proofs (Rocq development)
